  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan Crisis &#x2013; Response in health, nutrition, WASH, Education and child protection in conflict and displacement areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CERF is used to scale up response to immediate humanitarian needs arising due to the conflict between Sudanese Armed Forces (SAF) and Rapid Support Forces (RSF) that started on 15 April 2023. Since the beginning of the crisis, UNICEF has been responding in conflict zones as well as locations of displacement, and is preparing to scale up. UNICEF is prioritizing provision of life-saving and child protection engagements for the most vulnerable children and families in hotspots and areas of new displacement. This project targets a combined total of 260,000 affected people with engagements in the Health, Nutrition, WASH, EiE and Protection - CP sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
